What's different here:

Workflow status tracking - Not just data, but WHERE in the process
Audit fields - LastModifiedBy, LastModifiedDate, RowVersion
Soft delete - IsDeleted flag instead of actually deleting
Estimation handling - IsEstimate, EstimateReason (your new requirement)

The unique constraint:
(CountryID, TestTypeID, SubmissionMonth) WHERE IsDeleted = 0
This says: "One submission per country/test/month for active records."
Question for you: In your old system, could you have two records for the same country/test/month? How did you prevent duplicates?

Layer 3: The Many-to-Many Connectors (Junction Tables)
Look at Country_TestType and User_Country.
These are junction tables - they connect two entities that have a many-to-many relationship.
Country_TestType:

Says: "Korea offers Leadership Training and Data Analytics"
Says: "Japan doesn't offer Compliance Training"
Prevents invalid submissions: Can't submit volumes for test types not offered in that country
Has temporal tracking: When did Korea start offering this test?

User_Country:

Says: "Ji-Won is the primary coordinator for Korea"
Says: "John is the analyst for France, Japan, and Korea"
