Audit Trail vs Temporal Data (The Difference)
These concepts are related but serve different purposes. Let me clarify:
Temporal Data (Effective Dating)
Purpose: Track when SOMETHING WAS VALID
Question: "What was true on [date]?"
Example:

Korea offered Leadership Training from 2020-2024
Query: "What tests did Korea offer in 2023?" → Leadership Training

Focus: VERSIONS of truth over time

Audit Trail (Change History)
Purpose: Track WHO CHANGED WHAT, WHEN, and WHY
Question: "What changed, who changed it, and why?"
Example:

Ji-Won submitted Korea Nov volumes: Actual = 1000
John edited it: Actual = 950 (Reason: "Corrected double-count")
CFO asks: "Why did the number change?"

Focus: CHANGES and accountability

The Key Difference
Temporal Data:
"This record is valid from Date A to Date B"
Audit Trail:
"On Date X, User Y changed Field Z from Old Value to New Value because Reason"
Think of it this way:

Temporal Data = Timeline of what existed
Audit Trail = Log of what happened


