The Audit Trail Pattern (How It Works)
Look at Submission_History in the data model. Let me walk you through the fields:
Core Identity Fields
HistoryID (PK) - Unique ID for this history record
SubmissionID (FK) - Which submission this is about
ChangeDate - When the change happened
ChangedBy (FK → Users) - Who made the change
These answer: "WHEN and WHO"

Change Type Field
ChangeType - What kind of change?
  - "Created" (new submission)
  - "Updated" (data changed)
  - "Validated" (analyst reviewed)
  - "Rejected" (analyst rejected)
  - "Deleted" (marked as deleted)
  - "Restored" (un-deleted)
This answers: "WHAT happened at a high level"

Before/After Fields (The Critical Part)
PreviousStatus → NewStatus
PreviousActual → NewActual
PreviousBudget → NewBudget
PreviousForecast → NewForecast
These answer: "WHAT CHANGED specifically" (old value → new value)
Key principle: Store BOTH the old and new value so you can:

See what changed
Restore if needed
Reconstruct history


Reason Field
ChangeReason - WHY the change was made
This answers: "WHY" (the most important field for accountability)

Metadata Fields (Forensics)
IPAddress - Where the change came from
UserAgent - What browser/device
These answer: "HOW" (useful for security investigations)

