The Pattern: What Gets Audited?
Not everything needs audit trails. Focus on:
✅ Always Audit

Transactional data (Volume_Submissions)
Financial data (anything affecting reports)
Status changes (Draft → Submitted → Approved)
User assignments (who's responsible for what)
Configuration changes (system settings)

❌ Don't Usually Audit

Lookup data (Countries, TestTypes) - changes are rare
User profile info (display names) - not critical
System logs (already logged elsewhere)

Rule of thumb: If someone might ask "What changed and why?", audit it.

