Characteristics:

One row per measure change
Single value columns
Type dimension (Actual/Budget/Forecast)


Why I Chose Wide Format (And Why Yours Works Too)
Why I Chose Wide (Separate Columns)
Reason 1: Change Events Often Affect Multiple Measures
Real scenario: "Ji-Won submits November volumes"

Actual = 1000
Budget = 5000 (annual budget, submitted once)
Forecast = 2200

Wide format captures this as ONE event:
ChangeDate: 2025-11-01
ChangedBy: Ji-Won
NewActual: 1000
NewBudget: 5000
NewForecast: 2200
Narrow format requires THREE rows:
Row 1: Actual = 1000
Row 2: Budget = 5000
Row 3: Forecast = 2200
Trade-off: Wide = fewer rows, but more NULL values. Narrow = more rows, no NULLs.

Reason 2: Simpler Queries for "What Changed in This Event"
Question: "Show me everything that changed when John edited submission 523 on Nov 3"
Wide format query:
sqlSELECT 
  PreviousActual, NewActual,
  PreviousBudget, NewBudget,
  PreviousForecast, NewForecast
FROM Submission_History
WHERE SubmissionID = 523
  AND ChangeDate = '2025-11-03 14:30:00'
One row showing all changes.
Narrow format query:
sqlSELECT 
  LedgerType, 
  PreviousValue, 
  NewValue
FROM Submission_History
WHERE SubmissionID = 523
  AND ChangeDate = '2025-11-03 14:30:00'
```

**Multiple rows to reconstruct the event.**

