### Reason 2: Referential Integrity

**Scenario:** Submission 523 has child records
```
Volume_Submissions (SubmissionID: 523)
  ├── Submission_History (10 records referencing 523)
  ├── Data_Quality_Flags (3 records referencing 523)
  └── Communications (5 emails about 523)
```

**Hard Delete:**
```
Tries to delete submission 523
ERROR: Foreign key constraint violation
Cannot delete because child records exist

Options:
A) Delete all child records too (CASCADE DELETE) - loses everything
B) Can't delete at all - stuck with bad data
```

**Soft Delete:**
```
UPDATE IsDeleted = 1

All child records remain intact
All history preserved
All relationships intact
Can query "what happened to this submission?" even though it's deleted

