Validation:
Cannot be blank
Cannot be in distant past (e.g., before 2015)
Should be <= Today() for Active tests
Can be > Today() for Pending tests (future launch)
Use:

Prevents submissions before test existed
Historical analysis: "What tests were available in 2023?"
Reporting: "Show only tests effective as of [date]"

Query pattern (Power Apps):
javascript// Get tests available in March 2023
Filter(
  TestTypes,
  EffectiveDate <= Date(2023,3,31),
  Or(
    IsBlank(RetiredDate),
    RetiredDate > Date(2023,3,1)
  )
)
```

---

### RetiredDate (Date Column)

**Purpose:** When this test type was discontinued

**Nullable:** Yes (active tests have NULL RetiredDate)

**Examples:**
```
Old Leadership Course: 
  EffectiveDate: 2015-01-01
  RetiredDate: 2020-06-30
  Status: Retired
  
Current Analytics Course:
  EffectiveDate: 2023-01-01
  RetiredDate: NULL
  Status: Active
```

**Validation:**
```
If populated:
  RetiredDate >= EffectiveDate
  Status should = Retired
```

**Business rule:**
- When retiring a test, set RetiredDate to last day it was offered
- Status automatically becomes "Retired"
- Cannot delete test type if historical submissions exist
- Retired tests hidden from submission forms but visible in reports

**Use case:**
```
Scenario: Replacing old course with new version

Old Course:
  Title: "Leadership 1.0"
  EffectiveDate: 2015-01-01
  RetiredDate: 2025-12-31
  Status: Retired

New Course:
  Title: "Leadership 2.0"  
  EffectiveDate: 2026-01-01
  RetiredDate: NULL
  Status: Active
```

